# Separability of the full modular function field over L(j)

Theorem statement: `ModularCurve.isSeparable_adjoin_coeffEmb_jq_full`
(`d0d9ec31-a391-53e5-a27c-c93ffbc9fdf0`), by Claude, 2026-09-05.

Proof: submission `f70ee2ba-e9e0-5c2f-8322-1ac18b4a5277`, by Claude, 2026-09-05 (ACCEPTED); locally
adapted.

Let $L$ be a field equipped with a $\mathbb{Q}$-algebra structure and let $N$ be a nonzero natural
number. Write $jq \in \mathbb{Q}((q))$ for the Laurent series $q^{-1}$ times the power series
`jNumQ` obtained from `jNum` by coefficientwise reduction into $\mathbb{Q}$, and let
`modularFunctionFieldFull N` be the intermediate field of $\mathbb{Q}((q))$ generated over
$\mathbb{Q}$ by the set `divisorExpansions N`, i.e. by the elements `qExpand ℚ d jq` for the nonzero
divisors $d$ of $N$. Let `coeffEmb L` be the ring homomorphism $\mathbb{Q}((q)) \to L((q))$ applying
$\mathbb{Q} \to L$ to each coefficient, and let $E =$ `laurentBaseChange L (modularFunctionFieldFull
N)` be the intermediate field of $L((q))$ generated over $L$ by the image under `coeffEmb L` of
`modularFunctionFieldFull N`. Since `coeffEmb L jq` lies in $E$, it determines an element of $E$,
and one may form the intermediate field $X \subseteq E$ generated over $L$ by that single element.
The assertion is `Algebra.IsSeparable X E`: every element of $E$ is integral over $X$ with separable
minimal polynomial.

This is the separability of the covering of the $j$-line by the modular curve of level $N$, in the
base-changed Laurent-series model with constant field $L$ and with the ground field taken to be the
subfield generated by the single $q$-expansion of $j$. It is the hypothesis under which $dj$
generates the module of Kähler differentials of the modular function field, and it is used in the
treatment of differentials and $q$-expansions on modular curves.

